.TH ATHC 1 "2026-06-19" "athc 0.0.1" "~ATH Manual"
.SH NAME
athc \- compiler for the ~ATH esoteric language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B athc
.RI [ source.ath ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.RB [ \-\-compose
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-cc
.IR compiler ]
.RB [ \-\-emit\-ir ]
.RB [ \-\-emit\-obj
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-D
.IR name:min:max ]
.RB [ \-\-repl ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B athc
compiles ~ATH source files into native executables via LLVM IR and a
small C runtime. If no source file is given,
.B athc
starts an interactive REPL.
.PP
~ATH is an esoteric language where control flow is object liveness:
.B ~ATH(V) { ... }
loops while
.I V
is alive, and a program terminates by killing
.BR THIS .
.PP
The compile pipeline is: lex \(-> parse \(-> resolve imports \(-> semantic
analysis \(-> LLVM IR generation \(-> object emission \(-> link with C
runtime.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I source.ath
Path to the ~ATH source file. If omitted, the REPL is started.
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Write the output executable to
.IR output .
Default:
.BR a.out .
.TP
.B \-\-repl
Start the interactive REPL. Enabled automatically when no source
file is given.
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-ir
Print LLVM IR to stdout and exit. No object file or executable
is produced.
.TP
.BI \-\-emit\-obj " path"
Write the compiled object file to
.I path
and exit. No linking is performed.
.TP
.BI \-\-compose " mode"
Select the composition discipline for
.BR "BIFURCATE [L,R] V" .
.I mode
is one of:
.RS
.TP
.B fresh
Every compose allocates a new object. This is the default.
.TP
.B intern
Hash-consed by
.RI ( left , right )
pointer pair. Structurally equal composites share storage and
die together.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-runtime " path"
Path to the runtime library archive. By default,
.B athc
locates the bundled
.BI libath_ mode .a
from the installed package or the repository
.B runtime/
directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " compiler"
C compiler to use for linking. Default:
.BR gcc .
Overridden by the
.B CC
environment variable if the flag is not given.
.TP
.BI \-D " name\fR:\fImin\fR:\fImax"
.TQ
.BI \-\-define\-lifetime " name\fR:\fImin\fR:\fImax"
Register a custom library entry with a lifetime in seconds.
.I min
and
.I max
are non-negative floats with
.IR min " \(<= " max .
Spaces are permitted in
.IR name .
May be repeated.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CC
Default C compiler when
.B \-\-cc
is not specified. Falls back to
.BR gcc .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Compilation error (loader, semantic analysis, codegen, or invalid
arguments). A diagnostic with source location is printed to stderr.
.TP
.I nonzero
Linker failure propagates the linker's exit code.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile and run a program:
.PP
.nf
athc hello.ath -o hello && ./hello
.fi
.PP
Compile with interned composition:
.PP
.nf
athc program.ath -o program --compose intern
.fi
.PP
Dump LLVM IR:
.PP
.nf
athc program.ath --emit-ir
.fi
.PP
Start the REPL:
.PP
.nf
athc --repl
athc
.fi
.PP
Use clang as the linker:
.PP
.nf
athc program.ath -o program --cc clang
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B stdlib/*.ath
Standard library shims, resolved by
.BR "IMPORTF <name>" .
.TP
.B runtime/ath_runtime.h
ABI contract between codegen and the C runtime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ant (1)
